WEBVTT

NOTE Simplified English, written by hand from the Official Report by an AI assistant (Claude) in the developer's editor, not by the pipeline; not checked by a person. Timing: the verbatim track's cues, held for reading time where the gap allows.

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:12.006
Donald MacKinnon: A committee
has kept open a petition

00:00:12.006 --> 00:00:17.440
to end the guga hunt on
Sula Sgeir, in my area.

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:25.560
Does the First Minister agree the guga
hunt matters deeply to our culture?

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:32.227
Will the Government keep
the law that allows

00:00:32.227 --> 00:00:38.060
licences for taking
gannets from Sula Sgeir?

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:45.352
The First Minister: First, I
share the Presiding Officer's

00:00:45.352 --> 00:00:51.320
words about the death of Cathie
Craigie, a distinguished MSP.

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:54.540
I send my sympathy to her family,

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:57.340
the Labour Party and
colleagues across Parliament.

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:03.149
She was generous and kind to work with,

00:01:03.149 --> 00:01:07.620
and I thank her for her work.

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:15.580
On the question: the Government
has no plan to change the law.

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:23.220
NatureScot's decision was
about the scientific evidence.

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:28.733
That evidence is debated,

00:01:28.733 --> 00:01:33.827
but NatureScot was open

00:01:33.827 --> 00:01:38.920
about what it considered.

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:47.363
The decision about the 2026 hunt does not

00:01:47.363 --> 00:01:53.260
rule out applications for future years.

00:01:53.700 --> 00:02:01.004
I hope that helps Mr
MacKinnon's constituents,

00:02:01.004 --> 00:02:08.308
many of whom are worried about this.

00:02:08.308 --> 00:02:11.100
Helen McDade: Thank you, Presiding
Officer. Sorry about earlier.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:15.533
There are public inquiries
into NHS Tayside,

00:02:15.533 --> 00:02:21.233
where Sam Eljamel harmed
patients for nearly 20 years,

00:02:21.233 --> 00:02:24.400
and into a Glasgow hospital.

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:29.760
If those health boards are merged away,

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:35.120
how will anyone be held to account?

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:43.433
The First Minister: The
inquiries will continue.

00:02:43.433 --> 00:02:46.635
The NHS reorganisation

00:02:46.635 --> 00:02:53.040
will not stop or limit them.

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:58.940
Anything they find will be

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:03.660
dealt with by the

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:07.200
new NHS bodies,

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:13.100
if Parliament agrees the reforms.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:21.002
Fulton MacGregor: A domestic
abuse court advocate

00:03:21.002 --> 00:03:26.920
in Glasgow has told me
about planned pay changes.

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:31.050
Her salary could fall by about

00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:35.180
23 per cent from April 2028.

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:42.115
Will the First Minister talk to
Glasgow City Council so these

00:03:42.115 --> 00:03:48.420
changes do not harm support
for victims of domestic abuse?

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:56.100
The First Minister: There
are two separate issues.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:04:03.300
The first is pay and grading
at Glasgow City Council.

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:08.600
That is for the council to
decide, as the employer.

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:17.112
I know the concern about
the ASSIST project,

00:04:17.112 --> 00:04:22.094
but staff pay and grading

00:04:22.094 --> 00:04:26.080
are the council's matter.

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:33.492
The second issue is
steady funding for groups

00:04:33.492 --> 00:04:39.540
that tackle violence
against women and girls.

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:43.535
As I said two weeks ago,

00:04:43.535 --> 00:04:47.940
the Government is
committed to that funding.

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:51.640
I will say more in this
afternoon's debate.

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:58.760
Adam Harley: Lord Jim
Wallace campaigned on

00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:03.440
aortic dissection before
he died of it this year.

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:08.640
It kills over 2,000
people a year in the UK.

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:12.240
That number is expected to double by 2050.

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:20.080
Better awareness and a standard
care pathway would save lives.

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:27.040
Scotland has three specialist
centres, so we could lead the way.

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:34.103
In Jim Wallace's memory,
will the Government

00:05:34.103 --> 00:05:39.540
publish national guidelines
on aortic dissection?

00:05:42.060 --> 00:05:48.590
The First Minister: Mr Harley
has paid an outstanding

00:05:48.590 --> 00:05:55.120
tribute to Jim Wallace,
and I agree with him.

00:05:55.340 --> 00:06:02.100
I had great respect for Jim
Wallace and his public service.

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:08.434
When Neil Gray was health secretary,

00:06:08.434 --> 00:06:14.000
he met the trust to discuss these issues.

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:22.167
Where a condition needs
a clear care pathway,

00:06:22.167 --> 00:06:25.880
Scotland must have one.

00:06:25.880 --> 00:06:31.160
People must have access to

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:36.440
that pathway wherever they live.

00:06:36.440 --> 00:06:41.555
We will consider this, and I
will ask the health secretary,

00:06:41.555 --> 00:06:43.880
Angela Constance, to follow up.

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:48.280
She would be happy to meet
Mr Harley and the trust.

00:06:50.980 --> 00:06:57.437
Craig Hoy: Young people have been climbing
onto roofs in Dumfries town centre.

00:06:57.437 --> 00:06:59.920
It is called urban exploring.

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:04.730
The trend spreads on social media,

00:07:04.730 --> 00:07:09.540
worries residents and could cost lives.

00:07:10.020 --> 00:07:17.077
Will the First Minister help
warn people of the dangers,

00:07:17.077 --> 00:07:24.840
and will the Government work
with the police to tackle it?

00:07:25.940 --> 00:07:29.559
The First Minister:

00:07:29.559 --> 00:07:34.384
I understand the concern.

00:07:34.384 --> 00:07:39.209
It is another dangerous

00:07:39.209 --> 00:07:45.240
behaviour spread by social media.

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:52.560
I share Mr Hoy's concern, and the
Government will support Police Scotland.

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:59.511
Local police will act, but the council

00:07:59.511 --> 00:08:06.860
and schools will need to be involved too.

00:08:07.100 --> 00:08:12.479
It is probably not only
a problem in Dumfries.

00:08:12.479 --> 00:08:17.260
Mr Hoy is right to raise public awareness.

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:25.101
Katherine Sangster: Unions
say school support staff are

00:08:25.101 --> 00:08:29.977
not helped to deal with violent
behaviour by primary pupils.

00:08:29.977 --> 00:08:35.340
Edinburgh paid over £250,000 in
damages to support staff last year.

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:42.833
The council says that, with a £650
million gap in council budgets,

00:08:42.833 --> 00:08:46.580
it cannot deal with the problem.

00:08:48.260 --> 00:08:53.860
What will the First Minister do so
support staff do not face this alone?

00:08:54.980 --> 00:08:57.902
The First Minister:

00:08:57.902 --> 00:09:04.721
The answer is good behaviour in schools,

00:09:04.721 --> 00:09:11.540
for support staff,
teachers and pupils alike.

00:09:12.560 --> 00:09:20.320
The Government has set out many measures
to tackle behaviour in schools.

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:26.617
We are funding councils and working with

00:09:26.617 --> 00:09:31.740
unions so staff are always supported.

00:09:31.740 --> 00:09:38.927
I fully agree that good behaviour in

00:09:38.927 --> 00:09:44.060
schools matters for everyone's safety.

00:09:46.420 --> 00:09:50.791
Maggie Chapman: NHS Tayside plans to close

00:09:50.791 --> 00:09:55.787
Kingsway care centre in
Dundee in four months,

00:09:55.787 --> 00:10:03.280
moving dementia care to Forfar
and cutting beds by 36 per cent.

00:10:03.280 --> 00:10:06.580
Care for other vulnerable
adults will move too.

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:13.635
What does the First Minister
say to families who may need

00:10:13.635 --> 00:10:18.900
several bus journeys to visit
loved ones with dementia?

00:10:19.420 --> 00:10:24.100
Will he make sure nothing
changes without proper

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:28.780
consultation and proof
that care will not suffer?

00:10:30.760 --> 00:10:38.210
The First Minister: I
expect NHS Tayside to have

00:10:38.210 --> 00:10:45.660
considered the effect on each
resident before any move.

00:10:46.240 --> 00:10:49.670
Anyone whose care

00:10:49.670 --> 00:10:54.243
changes must have an

00:10:54.243 --> 00:10:59.960
individual assessment of their needs.

00:11:00.700 --> 00:11:05.580
I will ask the health secretary to

00:11:05.580 --> 00:11:10.460
make that clear to the health board.

00:11:10.460 --> 00:11:17.200
Sometimes services do
have to be redesigned.

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:22.113
From my own constituency work,

00:11:22.113 --> 00:11:27.217
I know we must sometimes modernise

00:11:27.217 --> 00:11:30.620
how services are delivered.

00:11:33.260 --> 00:11:38.444
But that must be centred
on each patient's needs.

00:11:38.444 --> 00:11:41.900
That is what I expect here.

00:11:47.180 --> 00:11:54.860
Angela Ross: Thursday's gas leak at
a planned battery site in Cockenzie

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:59.340
has added to worries about big energy

00:11:59.340 --> 00:12:03.180
sites close to homes and schools.

00:12:03.180 --> 00:12:09.187
The leak was caused by building
work, not the batteries.

00:12:09.187 --> 00:12:15.193
But should the national planning
rules be reviewed so such

00:12:15.193 --> 00:12:21.200
sites are in suitable places
and communities count for more?

00:12:23.860 --> 00:12:26.463
The First Minister:

00:12:26.463 --> 00:12:32.536
Any decision on where a facility goes

00:12:32.536 --> 00:12:36.874
must weigh every local factor

00:12:36.874 --> 00:12:42.080
and the effect on the community.

00:12:42.340 --> 00:12:45.540
That is essential in all
our planning policies.

00:12:46.240 --> 00:12:51.620
The national planning framework sets

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:58.076
the overall approach to land use,

00:12:58.076 --> 00:13:04.532
and all of this is considered

00:13:04.532 --> 00:13:07.760
in planning decisions.

00:13:08.280 --> 00:13:14.868
Also, whenever work is done on any site,

00:13:14.868 --> 00:13:22.280
the safety of the public
and workers comes first.

00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:26.370
That includes the Health and Safety

00:13:26.370 --> 00:13:30.460
Executive using its powers where needed.

00:13:34.120 --> 00:13:41.457
Calum Kerr: Yesterday, the First
Ministers met in Cardiff and agreed

00:13:41.457 --> 00:13:47.460
that our nations should decide
their own constitutional future.

00:13:48.220 --> 00:13:53.950
Last week, the Prime Minister
accepted that Scotland should have

00:13:53.950 --> 00:13:59.680
a referendum when people are
likely to vote for independence.

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:06.640
So what is the First Minister's next
step after the Cardiff agreement?

00:14:12.650 --> 00:14:20.293
The First Minister: It was good to
meet the First Ministers of Wales and

00:14:20.293 --> 00:14:27.390
Northern Ireland on the right of people
here to decide their own future.

00:14:28.090 --> 00:14:32.552
I welcome the Prime Minister's comments

00:14:32.552 --> 00:14:36.270
last Wednesday accepting that principle.

00:14:36.470 --> 00:14:43.150
It is about self-determination, and I
was glad to make that point yesterday.

00:14:43.830 --> 00:14:50.614
As for next steps: I want
Scotland to be able to decide its

00:14:50.614 --> 00:14:55.310
future in an independence referendum
in this parliamentary session.

00:14:55.950 --> 00:15:01.625
My office and the Government
will work to make

00:15:01.625 --> 00:15:06.670
sure people in Scotland
can decide by 2031.

00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:18.649
Kristopher Leask: Flights matter
to the Highlands and Islands,

00:15:18.649 --> 00:15:23.920
and I was glad the transport secretary
called a meeting on regional flights.

00:15:24.620 --> 00:15:31.940
But he is not attending his own meeting.
Will the First Minister go in his place?

00:15:35.980 --> 00:15:42.650
The First Minister: The cabinet
secretary has already stepped in,

00:15:42.650 --> 00:15:49.320
and he has kept a number of
flight services running.

00:15:49.640 --> 00:15:54.879
Government officials
will be at the meeting.

00:15:54.879 --> 00:15:58.621
Everything said there will go

00:15:58.621 --> 00:16:03.860
to ministers, who will act on it.

00:16:03.860 --> 00:16:10.886
Flights to our island communities
matter a great deal to me,

00:16:10.886 --> 00:16:14.080
and to the cabinet secretary.

00:16:17.820 --> 00:16:22.355
Jenni Minto: Tomorrow a charity
launches a women's health plan.

00:16:22.355 --> 00:16:29.612
Women are 50 per cent more likely than men
to be misdiagnosed after a heart attack,

00:16:29.612 --> 00:16:31.880
and have worse heart outcomes.

00:16:33.440 --> 00:16:39.756
What is the Government doing,
through its women's health plan,

00:16:39.756 --> 00:16:45.440
to improve women's heart health
and reduce those inequalities?

00:16:46.820 --> 00:16:50.420
The First Minister: First, I
recognise Jenni Minto's own

00:16:50.420 --> 00:16:54.820
work on the women's health
plan when she was a minister.

00:16:55.040 --> 00:16:59.040
The second phase of the
plan aims to tackle health

00:16:59.040 --> 00:17:02.240
inequalities for all women
and girls in Scotland.

00:17:02.560 --> 00:17:07.271
A heart health programme
has a women's strand,

00:17:07.271 --> 00:17:13.160
aimed at women who had high
blood pressure in pregnancy.

00:17:13.820 --> 00:17:19.180
Support has been designed with
charities to meet women's needs.

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:27.100
Early results show the care
pathway is working well.

00:17:27.100 --> 00:17:30.796
NHS staff have also been
trained on how women's

00:17:30.796 --> 00:17:33.260
reproductive health
affects later heart risk.

00:17:35.660 --> 00:17:42.620
Morven-May MacCallum: I declare
that I am a Highland councillor.

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:50.812
Sophie McNab, a young girl from
Inverness, needs residential care.

00:17:50.812 --> 00:17:55.199
She has been placed in Annan,

00:17:55.199 --> 00:17:58.855
230 miles from her family.

00:17:58.855 --> 00:18:01.780
She is not alone.

00:18:02.540 --> 00:18:08.131
26 Highland children live far from home,

00:18:08.131 --> 00:18:14.520
because there is no
suitable care in Highland.

00:18:15.090 --> 00:18:19.336
Does the First Minister
agree this is unacceptable?

00:18:19.336 --> 00:18:22.520
Will his Government bring them home?

00:18:25.380 --> 00:18:32.747
The First Minister: I agree
that children are best

00:18:32.747 --> 00:18:36.021
supported in their own

00:18:36.021 --> 00:18:40.933
family when it is safe —

00:18:40.933 --> 00:18:48.300
and, if not, as close to home as possible.

00:18:48.620 --> 00:18:54.700
That is part of the Promise, and the
Government is fully committed to it.

00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:57.440
We work closely with councils.

00:18:57.440 --> 00:19:01.192
As the member says,

00:19:01.192 --> 00:19:06.819
some areas may not have the

00:19:06.819 --> 00:19:10.571
right care nearby for

00:19:10.571 --> 00:19:15.260
the children who need it.

00:19:15.900 --> 00:19:22.954
So we must plan care across regions

00:19:22.954 --> 00:19:29.000
to meet each young person's needs.

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:32.868
The children's minister, Siobhian Brown,

00:19:32.868 --> 00:19:38.284
would be happy to discuss the Highland

00:19:38.284 --> 00:19:43.700
problem with the member and the council.

00:19:47.300 --> 00:19:51.705
Miles Briggs: Last Monday,

00:19:51.705 --> 00:19:58.313
two promising new breast cancer drugs

00:19:58.313 --> 00:20:03.820
were approved, offering real hope.

00:20:03.820 --> 00:20:11.061
England has had the drugs and the
genetic tests for over a year.

00:20:11.061 --> 00:20:14.961
In Scotland, patients
often cannot get them,

00:20:14.961 --> 00:20:18.860
because the tests are
not routinely available.

00:20:19.240 --> 00:20:21.455
It is not just breast cancer:

00:20:21.455 --> 00:20:24.407
since 2021, at least 15
other cancer medicines

00:20:24.407 --> 00:20:27.360
have been limited by a lack of testing.

00:20:27.360 --> 00:20:33.925
What interim help will
there be for these patients?

00:20:33.925 --> 00:20:41.220
And does Scotland need a lasting
plan for genetic testing?

00:20:51.620 --> 00:20:55.168
The First Minister: The
health secretary is looking

00:20:55.168 --> 00:20:58.715
at access to these treatments
after the approval.

00:20:58.715 --> 00:21:02.722
On genetic testing,

00:21:02.722 --> 00:21:08.064
last week I discussed

00:21:08.064 --> 00:21:13.406
strengthening our testing capacity,

00:21:13.406 --> 00:21:17.413
and good progress

00:21:17.413 --> 00:21:21.420
has been made.

00:21:23.000 --> 00:21:28.397
The chief scientist for
health, Dame Anna Dominiczak,

00:21:28.397 --> 00:21:33.120
is leading major work in this area.

00:21:36.440 --> 00:21:43.720
The specific issue is being looked at,
and testing in general is improving.

00:21:47.100 --> 00:21:54.360
I will write to Mr Briggs with details.

00:21:56.800 --> 00:22:03.242
Pauline Stafford: A 35-year-old man
died in Armadale at the weekend,

00:22:03.242 --> 00:22:07.926
reportedly in a targeted
attack with a gun.

00:22:07.926 --> 00:22:11.440
My thoughts are with his family.

00:22:11.840 --> 00:22:17.420
The police inquiry is ongoing, but
can the First Minister reassure

00:22:17.420 --> 00:22:23.000
people that everything is being
done to keep the community safe?

00:22:24.300 --> 00:22:25.895
The First Minister:

00:22:25.895 --> 00:22:33.340
I was sorry to hear about the
incident, and I am glad to comment.

00:22:33.880 --> 00:22:37.320
There is a live police investigation.

00:22:37.880 --> 00:22:42.125
Police Scotland has

00:22:42.125 --> 00:22:46.370
all the resources

00:22:46.370 --> 00:22:50.615
it needs to

00:22:50.615 --> 00:22:54.860
investigate the case.

00:22:55.520 --> 00:23:00.700
I assure Pauline Stafford
and her constituents

00:23:00.700 --> 00:23:06.620
that public safety comes
first for the police.

00:23:09.400 --> 00:23:16.900
Liam McArthur: Movember has published a
report on why men in Scotland die early.

00:23:17.520 --> 00:23:21.270
Men born in Scotland have the

00:23:21.270 --> 00:23:25.645
lowest life expectancy in the UK —

00:23:25.645 --> 00:23:30.645
77.4 years — and poorer areas fare worse.

00:23:30.645 --> 00:23:35.020
Does the First Minister share my alarm?

00:23:35.220 --> 00:23:41.320
If so, what will he do to improve
men's health in every community?

00:23:42.700 --> 00:23:48.953
The First Minister: I thank Mr McArthur.

00:23:48.953 --> 00:23:54.313
The report is a timely reminder

00:23:54.313 --> 00:23:58.780
that men's health must improve.

00:24:00.920 --> 00:24:04.960
The Government's programme focuses
on prevention and acting early.

00:24:05.160 --> 00:24:11.631
That means tackling alcohol and drug use,

00:24:11.631 --> 00:24:17.178
and helping men live healthier lives

00:24:17.178 --> 00:24:23.649
to reduce the risk of heart disease,

00:24:23.649 --> 00:24:30.120
stroke, lung cancer
and poor mental health.

00:24:30.120 --> 00:24:33.912
Shifting public services
towards prevention

00:24:33.912 --> 00:24:39.220
is meant to address exactly these issues.

00:24:41.880 --> 00:24:45.987
Amanda Lindsay: Will the First
Minister stop his Government

00:24:45.987 --> 00:24:50.549
calling the women who protested
at Glasgow Green "far right",

00:24:50.549 --> 00:24:57.850
and say what he will do about the failures
on women's safety that brought them there?

00:25:00.300 --> 00:25:01.784
The First Minister:

00:25:01.784 --> 00:25:08.217
I am leading a debate on violence
against women and girls this afternoon,

00:25:08.217 --> 00:25:11.680
and I want an open, honest discussion.

00:25:11.680 --> 00:25:18.680
But I will never stop confronting
the far right in this country.

00:25:27.190 --> 00:25:34.676
Lloyd Melville: Dundee and Angus
College plans a new campus in Arbroath —

00:25:34.676 --> 00:25:37.555
the town's biggest ever project.

00:25:37.555 --> 00:25:41.010
The SNP promised to support it.

00:25:41.010 --> 00:25:44.855
Can the First Minister update us on

00:25:44.855 --> 00:25:48.150
progress with the
Scottish Funding Council?

00:25:53.730 --> 00:25:55.243
The First Minister:

00:25:55.243 --> 00:26:00.790
The college has ambitious plans that
will affect Dundee and Arbroath.

00:26:01.910 --> 00:26:06.844
The Government has given the
Funding Council £2 million

00:26:06.844 --> 00:26:11.230
for colleges to develop
plans for major investment.

00:26:11.230 --> 00:26:18.670
Dundee and Angus College received £700,000
of that to work out the best option.

00:26:19.110 --> 00:26:23.510
The Government will follow the project
closely through the Funding Council.

00:26:26.110 --> 00:26:32.321
Martyn Day: About half of
Motability appeals succeed,

00:26:32.321 --> 00:26:37.756
but tribunals take 12 to 18 months.

00:26:37.756 --> 00:26:42.415
What will ministers ask the UK

00:26:42.415 --> 00:26:47.850
Government to do to cut these delays?

00:26:49.430 --> 00:26:54.810
The First Minister: We have raised this
important issue with the UK Government.

00:26:54.810 --> 00:26:59.770
For many people, a Motability

00:26:59.770 --> 00:27:07.706
car is the only way to get around,

00:27:07.706 --> 00:27:14.650
so support must come in good time.

00:27:15.370 --> 00:27:22.930
I will make sure the minister raises
it with the UK Government again.

00:27:25.270 --> 00:27:29.833
Holly Bruce: The site of Scotland's first

00:27:29.833 --> 00:27:34.396
national football ground
is in my constituency.

00:27:34.396 --> 00:27:38.307
Local people want to keep it

00:27:38.307 --> 00:27:42.870
as a community hub open to all.

00:27:43.510 --> 00:27:48.526
Should it be protected
and run by the community,

00:27:48.526 --> 00:27:51.870
not sold to the highest bidder?

00:27:56.390 --> 00:28:00.009
The First Minister: I am sympathetic.

00:28:00.009 --> 00:28:07.851
I want to give her an accurate
answer on who owns the site,

00:28:07.851 --> 00:28:15.090
so I will write to her with
what the Government can do.

00:28:16.340 --> 00:28:21.860
David Linden: The First Minister mentioned

00:28:21.860 --> 00:28:27.380
men's health and the Movember report.

00:28:27.380 --> 00:28:34.740
Men's sheds help bring
these issues to light.

00:28:35.160 --> 00:28:38.896
Will the First Minister
visit Shettleston Men's

00:28:38.896 --> 00:28:43.700
Shed to see how such
spaces help men's health?

00:28:45.900 --> 00:28:50.020
The First Minister: I
would be happy to visit.

00:28:50.020 --> 00:28:55.780
I have visited several,

00:28:55.780 --> 00:29:01.540
most recently in Renfrew.

00:29:02.100 --> 00:29:08.787
Men's sheds help men meet

00:29:08.787 --> 00:29:12.800
and overcome loneliness.

00:29:12.800 --> 00:29:17.757
It is a great movement.

00:29:17.757 --> 00:29:22.714
I look forward to visiting

00:29:22.714 --> 00:29:26.680
Shettleston with Mr Linden.

00:29:29.740 --> 00:29:35.880
Michael Marra: Women in Tayside face
severe problems getting gynaecology care.

00:29:36.440 --> 00:29:42.249
NHS Tayside says year-long
waits fell from 1,348 to 11.

00:29:42.249 --> 00:29:49.800
That is simply not true — many of
my constituents have waited years.

00:29:50.080 --> 00:29:54.057
One was told she would wait over
three years for a hysterectomy.

00:29:54.057 --> 00:29:59.360
She took out a loan to go private and
never made it onto the waiting list.

00:29:59.360 --> 00:30:03.760
Does the First Minister think these
waits in Tayside are acceptable?

00:30:05.300 --> 00:30:11.162
The First Minister: Waiting
times must come down everywhere.

00:30:11.162 --> 00:30:16.372
Mr Marra raises an important
point about Tayside,

00:30:16.372 --> 00:30:20.280
and I want those waits cut.

00:30:20.800 --> 00:30:25.560
I will check the figures he doubts,

00:30:25.560 --> 00:30:28.960
because they must be accurate.

00:30:31.180 --> 00:30:36.927
The health secretary and I
review waiting lists every week,

00:30:36.927 --> 00:30:39.800
by specialty and by area.

00:30:40.440 --> 00:30:47.029
Some areas wait much less than

00:30:47.029 --> 00:30:52.520
others for the same treatment.

00:30:52.940 --> 00:30:58.060
That is one reason the

00:30:58.060 --> 00:31:03.180
Government is reforming the NHS.

00:31:03.180 --> 00:31:09.412
We want to remove health
board boundaries that stand in

00:31:09.412 --> 00:31:15.020
the way of fair treatment
for Mr Marra's constituents.

00:31:17.360 --> 00:31:21.699
I will look at those figures,

00:31:21.699 --> 00:31:26.761
but the health secretary and I examine

00:31:26.761 --> 00:31:31.100
progress on waiting times every week.

00:31:31.100 --> 00:31:37.020
This issue matters greatly to me.

00:31:38.180 --> 00:31:39.880
The Presiding Officer:
Thank you, First Minister.

00:31:39.880 --> 00:31:44.680
I apologise to the 28 backbench
members I could not call today.
